---
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '~/consts';
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '~/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import type { Crumb } from '~/types';

const crumbs: Crumb[] = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Terms' }];
const updated = 'September 24, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that apply when you use ByteCabin's free developer tools, including the limits of warranty and acceptable use."
  canonical="/terms"
>
  <div class="py-6 sm:py-8">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="bc-prose mt-6">
      <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These terms apply to your use of {SITE.domain} and the tools it provides. Using the site
        means you accept them. If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The service</h2>
      <p>
        ByteCabin provides free developer utilities that run in your web browser. No account is
        required and no payment is taken. We may add, change, or remove tools at any time, and we
        may stop providing the service altogether.
      </p>

      <h2>3. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>The tools are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind.</strong> We work hard
        to make them correct, but we do not guarantee that any tool is free of errors, that its
        output is accurate or fit for a particular purpose, or that the site will be available
        without interruption.
      </p>
      <p>
        This matters in practice. Do not rely on a ByteCabin tool as the only check on something
        important. In particular: a successful JWT signature verification here does not replace
        proper verification in your application; a hash computed here should be confirmed with
        your platform's own tooling before it gates a release; and generated passwords should be
        stored in a password manager rather than trusted to a browser tab.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, ByteCabin and its operators are not liable for any
        direct, indirect, incidental, consequential or special damages arising from your use of,
        or inability to use, the site — including data loss, lost profits, or business
        interruption. Because the service is free, the total liability for any claim is limited to
        zero.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          use the site to process data you do not have the right to process, or for any unlawful
          purpose
        </li>
        <li>
          attempt to disrupt the site, its hosting infrastructure, or other people's use of it
        </li>
        <li>
          scrape or automate the site at a volume that degrades it for others; the content is
          static and cheap to serve, but sustained automated traffic is not what it is for
        </li>
        <li>
          misrepresent ByteCabin output as certified, audited, or as a substitute for professional
          security or legal advice
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Your data</h2>
      <p>
        The content you enter into a tool stays in your browser and is not transmitted to us. You
        remain responsible for it, including for ensuring you are permitted to process it. See the
        <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for the full picture.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The ByteCabin name, logo, site design and written explanations on tool pages are owned by
        the operators of the site. The output a tool produces from your input is yours — we claim
        no rights over it. You may not copy the site's explanatory content wholesale for a
        competing site.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        Pages may link to external documentation and specifications. We do not control those sites
        and are not responsible for their content or their privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The site may display advertising in future. Where it does, ads will be clearly labelled
        and visually separated from tool controls. Any transaction you enter into with an
        advertiser is between you and them.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The "last updated" date above will change when we do, and
        continued use of the site after that date means you accept the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.general}`}>{CONTACT.general}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
